Package: topicsovertime
Type: Package
Title: Topics over Time: A Continuous-Time Topic Model
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jaeseong", "Choe", email = "cjssoote@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Fits the Topics over Time model of Wang and McCallum (2006)
    <doi:10.1145/1150402.1150450>, a latent Dirichlet allocation style topic
    model in which each topic also has a Beta distribution over continuous
    time, so topics are shaped by both word co-occurrence and document
    timestamps without discretizing time or assuming Markov dynamics.
    Inference uses collapsed Gibbs sampling implemented in 'C++'. Includes
    prediction of topic proportions and timestamps for new documents, topic
    trends over time, and simulation of synthetic corpora.
